  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vikash Lodhi vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 21 November, 2025 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: G. S. Ahluwalia Neutral Citation No. 2025:Mphc-Gwl:30978 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Gwalior Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice G. S. Ahluwalia On The 21st Of November, 2025 Miscellaneous Second Appeal No. 33 of 2025 Vikash Lodhi And Others Versus The State Of Madhya Pradesh Appearance: Shri Anil Kumar Sharma, Advocate for appellants. Shri S.S.Kushwah, Government Advocate for respondent/State Judgment",
    "facts": "This miscellaneous second appeal, under section 71(6) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short \"FSSA\") has been filed against the judgment dated 15/5/2025 passed by Principal District Judge, Gwalior/ Appellate Authority in RCA No. 93/2025, as well as, order dated 27/12/2024 passed by Adjudicating Officer/Additional District Magistrate Gwalior in case No. Q/Food safety/05/2024. It is not out of place to mention here that the Adjudicating Officer had imposed a penalty of Rs.3,00,000/- after holding the appellant guilty under section 51 of FSSA. 2. Facts necessary for disposal of present appeal, in short, are that a complaint was filed before the Adjudicating Officer contending that on 16/6/2023, at about 1:00 p.m., the Food Safety Officer had inspected the Firm M/s Hanuman Dairy. Appellant No.1 was present at the time of inspection and he disclosed that Ravi Lodhi is the proprietor, who is his elder brother. During inspection, it was found that 2 kg of Paneer and 5 kg of Mawa were kept in loose NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2025:MPHC-GWL:30978 2 MSA-33-2025 condition. The sample of Mawa and Paneer were taken by the Food Safety Officer with consent of appellant No.1. After completing the formalities, the sealed samples were sent to Food Laboratory, Bhopal. As per the reports (Ex.P/15 and P/19), both the samples were found to be substandard. Thereafter a notice under section 46(4) of FSSA was given thereby intimating the appellants that they can file an appeal against the report of Food Vikash Lodhi vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 21 November, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/38666752/ 1 Analyst, but they did not file any appeal. The sanction for prosecution was obtained and accordingly complaint was filed. 3. Appellants appeared before the Adjudicating Officer and refuted the allegations and claimed that they had not committed any offence and no raid was conducted in their premises. 4. It is the case of appellants that the appellants are petty traders and the penalty amount may be reduced.",
